courses.learning_outcomes:
Student should be able to:

* Learn about the history and development of globalization, the foundational concepts and frameworks of global health policy, governance, justice, and the right to health
* Understand the key concepts of poverty and social determinants of global health inequalities
* Learn about the foundations of health demography, especially the impact of demographic dynamics of urbanization and migration on global health and policies;
* Understand the financing of political economy of global health, and the multi-lateral foreign aid and corruption relevant to global health programs;
* Understand the impact of globalization on food security;
* Understand the global health policy’s responses to world’s rare and neglected diseases
